# `{{dashCase name}}` Engineering Constitution (Angular 21 Signals Web App)

## 1. Pure Functional Core & Signals State (`ADR-007`)
- Keep domain transformations and route/auth state evaluation in pure, deterministic TypeScript functions.
- Use Angular 21 standalone components (`standalone: true`), `signal()`, `computed()`, and modern `@if` / `@for` / `@switch` control flow. Legacy `*ngIf` / `*ngFor` / `*ngSwitch` directives are forbidden.

## 2. Shared Configuration & Auth Slot
- TypeScript extends `../../packages/config/tsconfig.angular.json` (`@cmp/config`).
- ESLint flat config extends `angular` from `../../packages/config/eslint.config.mjs`.
- Authentication plugs into `src/app/auth/auth.slot.ts` (`AUTH_SLOT` / `provideAuthSlot()`), keeping OAuth/session providers decoupled from UI components.

## 3. Verification Gate
Before any change is considered complete, all of the following must pass:
- `npm run lint`
- `npm run typecheck`
- `npm run build`
- `npm test`
